{"name":"Sherwood Forest","hex":"#555a4c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sherwood Forest","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A country park in Nottinghamshire, England.","The banks of Polaris missile tubes on a submarine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sherwood_Forest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sherwood Forest","blocks":[{"text":"Sherwood Forest consists of the remnants of an ancient royal forest in Nottinghamshire, in the East Midlands region of England. It is associated with the legend of Robin Hood. The forest was proclaimed by William the Conqueror and mentioned in the Domesday Book in 1086. The reserve has the highest concentration of ancient trees in Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Sherwood_Forest%2C_May%2C_2017-5.jpg/330px-Sherwood_Forest%2C_May%2C_2017-5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherwood_Forest"},{"title":"Sherwood Forest (constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"Sherwood Forest is a constituency represented in the House of Commons of the UK Parliament since 2024 by Michelle Welsh, of the Labour Party. The constituency's name is shared with Sherwood Forest, which is in the area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/East_Midlands_-_Sherwood_Forest_constituency.svg/330px-East_Midlands_-_Sherwood_Forest_constituency.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherwood_Forest_(constituency)"},{"title":"Forest","blocks":[{"text":"A forest is an ecosystem characterized by a dense community of trees. Hundreds of definitions of forest are used throughout the world, incorporating factors such as tree density, tree height, land use, legal standing, and ecological function. The United Nations' Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) defines a forest as, \"Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban use.\" Using this definition, Global Forest Resources Assessment 2025 found that forests covered 4.14 billion hectares, or approximately 31 percent of the world's land area in 2025."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg/330px-Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/The_Major_Oak_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1691865.jpg/500px-The_Major_Oak_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1691865.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/The_Major_Oak_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1691865.jpg/500px-The_Major_Oak_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1691865.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Major_Oak_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1691865.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Robin_Hood_Statue%2C_Sherwood_Forest.jpg/500px-Robin_Hood_Statue%2C_Sherwood_Forest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Robin_Hood_Statue%2C_Sherwood_Forest.jpg/1280px-Robin_Hood_Statue%2C_Sherwood_Forest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Robin_Hood_Statue%2C_Sherwood_Forest.jpg/500px-Robin_Hood_Statue%2C_Sherwood_Forest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Robin Hood Statue, Sherwood Forest","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fil